{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChPK7pTRoXzrPvzzEmcWX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"A merge now keeps a stale review or approval covering the PR only if its tree equals git's clean merge of its two parents. This applies to every merge in the chain.\n\nWhitespace edits, hand-resolved conflicts and hand-crafted merges break the cover. If `merge-tree --write-tree` fails or is missing, the PR is treated as not covered. A genuine clean update merge that touches a shared file with different hunks stays covered.\n\nI ran `go build ./...`, `go vet`, gofmt and `go test` on the gitx, prgate, merger, reviewfix and reviewer packages, and all pass. I did not run `make lint` or `make test`. I added no separate merger-package approval test, because the approval check goes through `CoversDetail`, which the prgate tests with real repos exercise.\n\n- **Check:** `MergeTreeEqual` in `internal/gitx/inspect.go` runs `merge-tree --write-tree` with attributes from the empty tree, no rerere and no renormalize.\n- **Gate:** `firstUpdateMerge` in `internal/prgate/prgate.go` now calls it on each merge it walks. `internal/merger/loop.go` only needed the interface widened.\n- **Docs:** the merger cover paragraph in `docs/proposal.md` is corrected.\n\nTests cover whitespace changes in `.py`, `.yaml` and Makefile files, a hand-crafted merge, a chain whose second merge is non-mechanical, and a stub git that rejects `merge-tree`.\n\nAs the plan decided, I kept the patch-id comparison and did not add a raw-diff hash. A clean merge authored by ard itself is indistinguishable from any other clean merge, so it stays covered.\n\nThe report is in `.ard/366/worker-engineer.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":970,"cache_read_input_tokens":41975,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":970}